{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "bcfb0feb-77b4-8c47-af78-ccd7e380989a",
  "created_at": "2026-01-05T09:34:32-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Canvassing",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Andres N. Cordero",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Walter Tavares",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:29:32-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good morning, City of Newport Canvassing, this is Walter. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:29:39-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hey, good morning. Yeah, I had a question about voter registration. It's kind of a specific one."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:29:47-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:29:49-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "So there's a student, a college student, and they live in the dorms up on campus. Can they register to vote at the campus address? Or does it have to be a home address somewhere else?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:30:05-05:00",
      "duration": 26,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good question. A student can register where they actually live, so if the dorm is their residence while they're at school, they can use the campus address. They'd list the building and room, and the mailing address if that's different. They can also choose to stay registered at their parents' address if that's still their home. It's one or the other, not both."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:30:31-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, okay. So it's their choice, basically."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:30:35-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right. Whichever one they consider their primary residence. The main thing is they can't be registered in two places."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:30:44-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. And is there like, a deadline for that? Like a cutoff before an election?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:30:51-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, there's a cutoff before each election. It's about a month out, give or take. I'd rather not give you a day that's off, because it depends on which election you're talking about. Is this for a particular one?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:31:08-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Um, not really a particular one. Just whatever's coming up next, I guess. I figured I'd find out now so I'm not scrambling."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:31:18-05:00",
      "duration": 22,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That makes sense. The best thing is to check the state elections website, they post the dates for every election, or you can call us back once the next one is scheduled and we'll tell you the exact date. Registering sooner is always safe. If they register now, they're set for whatever comes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:31:40-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wicked, that works. Can they do it online, or do they have to come in?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:31:47-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Either. There's an online registration through the state if they have a Rhode Island license or ID. Otherwise they can fill out a paper form, mail it, or drop it off here at City Hall."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:32:02-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Totally. And what if they don't have a Rhode Island ID? Like if their license is from out of state."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:32:11-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Then the paper form is the way to go. They'd put the last four digits of their Social Security number, or they can use another form of ID. We can go over what's needed when they come in, it's pretty simple."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:32:29-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Sorry, one sec. My cousin's texting me again. He keeps asking to borrow a little cash, every other week it's something. I'm not answering that right now."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:32:41-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:32:44-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, all good. So the paper form, where do I get one? Or where does the student get one, I mean."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:32:54-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "We have them at the front counter here at City Hall, and they can be printed from the state website too. We're open weekdays during regular business hours."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:33:06-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Perfect. And does the student need to bring proof that they live in the dorm? Like a letter from the school?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:33:16-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Not usually for registering. They just write down where they live. If there's ever a question, a housing letter or a school ID with the address can help, but it's not a standard requirement at the counter."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:33:32-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, that's easier than I figured. And if they move rooms or move off campus later?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:33:39-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "They'd just update their registration with the new address. Same form, there's a box to check for a change of address. It's best to do it before the cutoff for whichever election is next."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:33:54-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Alright. So to sum up, campus address is fine if they live there, only one registration, form online or paper, and check the state site for the date."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:34:06-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's exactly right. And you're welcome to call us back if anything comes up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:34:13-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great. Do you need my number or anything?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:34:17-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, you're all set. I don't need to follow up on anything."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:34:23-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Thanks a lot, Walter. Appreciate the help."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:34:27-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome. Have a good Monday."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-05T09:34:30-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Bye."
    }
  ],
